{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FIX LANDED: Gerrit change 2140, merged as 59fad3133f9 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, no unresolved comments). maybe_drain's gate now calls queue.has_pending_enrichment — an existence-only probe that walks the same candidates (marker live set, else full store) with the same reduce_ticket pending predicate but early-exits at the FIRST pending hit; a quiet full walk still writes the gate marker.\n\nBEFORE/AFTER, measured on the live store (5,269 tickets, 1,026 pending backlog, this host):\n- steady state (marker-scoped, the per-write case): 2,792.8-7,557.5 ms -> 1.0-1.5 ms — inside the 20 ms budget (was 140-378x over).\n- cold path (no marker, first probe after a queue append): 6,773.9 ms -> 117.5 ms.\n- during this session, before the fix, live commands paid: claim 7,375.8 ms, comment 9,097.9 ms gate checks.\n\nWarning rate: the steady-state probe meets the budget, so the per-command warning is gone. A cold probe (marker cleared by a queue append) may still exceed 20 ms once (~117 ms here); the drain's own pending_enrichment full walk rewrites the marker, so overruns are bounded to post-queue-append probes, not per-command — satisfying AC2's 'meets its budget or warns at a bounded, non-per-command rate'.\n\nRegression pins landed with the fix (tests/unit/test_enrich_queue.py): scan-count test proving ONE reduction per backlogged probe at any backlog size (marker-scoped AND cold paths, counted not timed, mirroring test_pin_health_store_scan_count.py), a verdict-equivalence test pinning has_pending_enrichment == bool(pending_enrichment) across every reducer-distinguished queue state, and a quiet-repeat O(1) test.\n\nOut of scope, still open under the option-2 design track (relates_to 9c72): drain throughput/lock-hold (LLM calls inside the advisory lock, batch cap 5) and the standing ~1,050-entry backlog policy."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787451942243411001,"uuid":"07e47abf-5b44-4a4e-97c1-acda3ded7638"}